<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6531" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cănor</span></b> , ōris, m.
		cano, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>tune</i>, <i>sound</i>, <i>song</i>, <i>melody</i> (<b>poet.</b> or in post-Aug. prose; rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Of living beings, <i><span class="en">Quint. 1,
				10, 22</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cygni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					4, 182</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">4, 911</span></i>: res
			est blanda canor; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">discant cantare puellae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. A.
					A. 3, 315</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mulcendas natus ad aures,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. M.
					5, 561</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Of
			instruments, <i>the tone</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Martius aeris rauci canor,</span>”
				<i>martial clang</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 4, 71</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lyrae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					H. 16, 180</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bella truci memorata canore,</span>”
				<i>in heroic poetry</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 5, 19</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
